Quiz02_01: 50 points
(FnA1szLongestMonoSubsequence)
Please state the status of this question:

1. Incomplete
2. Solved with testing?
3. Solved without testing?
   If solved, please BRIEFLY explain your strategy.

Solved with testing.
The implementation is in O(n^2) time as it utilizes a nested for loop where the outer loop iterates through each position i (n iterations), and the inner loop checks all previous positions j < i (averaging n/2 iterations). Each comparison and update inside the loops takes constant O(1) time. So, the total number of operations is approximately n x (n/2) = n^2/2, which simplifies to O(n^2). All other operations involving loops are O(n), which is dominated by the O(n^2) nested loops.

STRATEGY:
For each position i, check all previous positions j < i to find the longest ascending subsequence ending at j that can be extended by including element i. Store the best length and parent pointer at each position. After filling the DP table, find the position with maximum length (scanning left-to-right ensures leftmost), then reconstruct the subsequence by following parent pointers backward.
